WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.875 --> 00:00:30.041


2
00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:32.375
<b>Here, Lord Krishna says</b>

3
00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:35.000
<b>that this body is also not permanent;</b>

4
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.625
<b>it keeps changing.</b>

5
00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:38.750
<b>The body in which the soul resides</b>

6
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:45.708
<b>also passes through the stages</b>
<b>of childhood, youth, and old age,</b>

7
00:00:45.708 --> 00:00:46.750
<b>and finally,</b>

8
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.916
<b>when this body is destroyed,</b>

9
00:00:48.916 --> 00:00:54.041
<b>the soul simply finds a new home, a new body.</b>

10
00:00:54.041 --> 00:00:57.875
<b>Those who know this, the patient and</b>
<b>intelligent individuals,</b>

11
00:00:57.875 --> 00:01:03.375
<b>do not get confused by the attachment to</b>
<b>this body, this physical form.</b>

12
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.208


13
00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:13.416
<b>At this moment, such doubts might</b>
<b>be arising in Arjuna's mind.</b>

14
00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:14.458
<b>Perhaps</b>

15
00:01:14.458 --> 00:01:16.875
<b>you have the same doubts in your mind.</b>

16
00:01:16.875 --> 00:01:19.791
<b>That even if our true existence is a soul,</b>

17
00:01:19.791 --> 00:01:23.000
<b>for which this body is only a medium,</b>

18
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.375
<b>isn't it still natural</b>

19
00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:28.333
<b>for us to have an attachment</b>
<b>to our current body</b>

20
00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:32.041
<b>and to grieve at the destruction of this body?</b>

21
00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:38.291
<b>Lord Krishna addresses this doubt by discussing</b>
<b>the constant change of the human body.</b>

22
00:01:38.291 --> 00:01:39.125
<b>Because</b>

23
00:01:39.125 --> 00:01:42.666
<b>our body is being destroyed every moment.</b>

24
00:01:42.666 --> 00:01:48.000
<b>Every moment, countless cells of</b>
<b>this perishable body die,</b>

25
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.750
<b>and many new cells are born.</b>

26
00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:57.166
<b>It is through this death and birth of</b>
<b>cells that the state of the body changes.</b>

27
00:01:57.166 --> 00:01:58.666
<b>In childhood</b>

28
00:01:58.666 --> 00:02:00.000
<b>and youth,</b>

29
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.041
<b>when the number of cell births exceeds</b>
<b>the number of cell deaths,</b>

30
00:02:04.041 --> 00:02:05.666
<b>the body grows,</b>

31
00:02:05.666 --> 00:02:07.583
<b>and strength increases.</b>

32
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:08.625
<b>But</b>

33
00:02:08.625 --> 00:02:12.583
<b>then in old age, when this equation reverses,</b>

34
00:02:12.583 --> 00:02:16.583
<b>the body also slowly starts</b>
<b>moving towards destruction.</b>

35
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:17.625
<b>If you look at it,</b>

36
00:02:17.625 --> 00:02:21.125
<b>our body is constantly being destroyed</b>

37
00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:23.458
<b>and constantly being reborn.</b>

38
00:02:23.458 --> 00:02:28.958
<b>Any change that we know about</b>
<b>beforehand does not cause distress.</b>

39
00:02:28.958 --> 00:02:30.916
<b>Every day, the sun rises,</b>

40
00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:34.250
<b>then evening comes, and then night.</b>

41
00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:38.291
<b>We don't get distressed thinking,</b>
<b>why did the sun go away,</b>

42
00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.041
<b>why did darkness fall?</b>

43
00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:45.666
<b>This is because we have the</b>
<b>knowledge that this will happen every day,</b>

44
00:02:45.666 --> 00:02:49.458
<b>and how can we be anxious about</b>
<b>something that happens every day? </b>

45
00:02:49.458 --> 00:02:50.500
<b>Similarly,</b>

46
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.583
<b>there is a need here for us to raise our level</b>

47
00:02:53.583 --> 00:02:56.583
<b>and understand this excellent knowledge.</b>

48
00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:59.291
<b>We should not grieve over</b>
<b>the changes in the body,</b>

49
00:02:59.291 --> 00:03:03.875
<b>just as we do not grieve over the</b>
<b>daily changes of morning, evening, and night.</b>

50
00:03:03.875 --> 00:03:04.708
<b>Why?</b>

51
00:03:04.708 --> 00:03:07.291
<b>Because we know about it beforehand.</b>

52
00:03:07.291 --> 00:03:09.791
<b>So just understand this as well</b>

53
00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:14.750
<b>just as the cycle of morning, evening,</b>
<b>and night will continue,</b>

54
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:19.541
<b>the cycle of cells dying and living will continue,</b>

55
00:03:19.541 --> 00:03:20.583
<b>in the same way,</b>

56
00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:21.875
<b>the death of the body</b>

57
00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:27.208
<b>and the soul changing bodies will</b>
<b>also continue for eternity.</b>

58
00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:30.625
<b>And why grieve over what will continue? </b>

59
00:03:30.625 --> 00:03:34.250
<b>Why grieve over what is known?</b>

60
00:03:34.875 --> 00:03:38.625


61
00:03:38.625 --> 00:03:44.000
<b>In this transient world, we yearn for stability.</b>

62
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.416
<b>Where every moment our body is dying</b>
<b>and taking birth simultaneously,</b>

63
00:03:49.416 --> 00:03:58.625
<b>we expect this ever-changing body to</b>
<b>remain constant, to stay alive forever.</b>

64
00:03:58.625 --> 00:04:00.708
<b>The truth is,</b>

65
00:04:00.708 --> 00:04:06.166
<b>we close our eyes in attachment</b>
<b>to this mortal frame.</b>

66
00:04:06.166 --> 00:04:09.333
<b>For it is known to all</b>

67
00:04:09.333 --> 00:04:15.458
<b>that one day, death will come</b>
<b>and take this body away.</b>

68
00:04:15.458 --> 00:04:18.666
<b>If we truly open our eyes,</b>

69
00:04:18.666 --> 00:04:21.166
<b>we will gain knowledge of this truth,</b>

70
00:04:21.166 --> 00:04:24.541
<b>and then we shall find the stability we seek.</b>

71
00:04:24.541 --> 00:04:28.291
<b>That stability lies within our soul.</b>

72
00:04:28.291 --> 00:04:32.041
<b>It is this soul that will persist eternally.</b>

73
00:04:32.041 --> 00:04:36.333
<b>This is the only unchanging </b>
<b>element in the universe.</b>

74
00:04:36.333 --> 00:04:37.458
<b>Therefore,</b>

75
00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:41.458
<b>rise above the illusion of</b>
<b>ever-changing materiality,</b>

76
00:04:41.458 --> 00:04:43.750
<b>turn towards spirituality,</b>

77
00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.916
<b>engage in actions that satisfy your soul,</b>

78
00:04:46.916 --> 00:04:48.583
<b>read such articles, </b>

79
00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:50.458
<b>listen to such discourses.</b>

80
00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:52.333
<b>And then,</b>

81
00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:56.833
<b>witness an unprecedented</b>
<b>experience of stability in life.</b>

82
00:04:57.375 --> 00:05:01.125


83
00:05:01.125 --> 00:05:05.166
<b>This scene is never unfamiliar,</b>

84
00:05:05.166 --> 00:05:06.416
<b>where an elder</b>

85
00:05:06.416 --> 00:05:09.958
<b>asks a little child,</b>

86
00:05:09.958 --> 00:05:11.708
<b>"Where is your nose?</b>

87
00:05:11.708 --> 00:05:13.041
<b>Touch your nose and show me.</b>

88
00:05:13.041 --> 00:05:14.916
<b>Where are your ears?</b>

89
00:05:14.916 --> 00:05:17.708
<b>What is your name?"</b>

90
00:05:17.708 --> 00:05:24.916
<b>From childhood, we build our</b>
<b>identity around this body.</b>

91
00:05:24.916 --> 00:05:26.750
<b>But</b>

92
00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:29.666
<b>what is this body?</b>

93
00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:35.458
<b>If you ask this question to</b>
<b>a biologist or a physician,</b>

94
00:05:35.458 --> 00:05:38.416
<b>they might say that</b>

95
00:05:38.416 --> 00:05:43.083
<b>this body is made up of numerous chemicals.</b>

96
00:05:43.083 --> 00:05:44.166
<b>But</b>

97
00:05:44.166 --> 00:05:50.416
<b>is this body merely a mixture of</b>
<b>substances and chemicals?</b>

98
00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:55.083
<b>This doesn't seem to define</b>
<b>our existence, does it?</b>

99
00:05:55.083 --> 00:05:57.125
<b>So, what is the truth?</b>

100
00:05:57.125 --> 00:06:00.166
<b>Who are we?</b>

101
00:06:00.166 --> 00:06:03.291
<b>We are simply a soul,</b>

102
00:06:03.291 --> 00:06:11.166
<b>wearing the garment of this body,</b>
<b>living in this world.</b>

103
00:06:11.166 --> 00:06:13.125
<b>Have you ever pondered</b>

104
00:06:13.125 --> 00:06:18.833
<b>that as we grow older,</b>
<b>our body completely changes?</b>

105
00:06:18.833 --> 00:06:25.500
<b>In youth, many people fail to</b>
<b>recognize us from our childhood photos.</b>

106
00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.625
<b>But</b>

107
00:06:26.625 --> 00:06:28.750
<b>does this change in the body</b>

108
00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:33.958
<b>alter our affection towards our loved ones?</b>

109
00:06:33.958 --> 00:06:35.666
<b>No, right?</b>

110
00:06:35.666 --> 00:06:37.916
<b>Why is that?</b>

111
00:06:37.916 --> 00:06:41.291
<b>Because if the body was our existence,</b>

112
00:06:41.291 --> 00:06:46.916
<b>then changing the body would also</b>
<b>change the love for our family, wouldn't it?</b>

113
00:06:46.916 --> 00:06:51.458
<b>The reason is that we love not the body,</b>

114
00:06:51.458 --> 00:06:52.208
<b>but</b>

115
00:06:52.208 --> 00:06:59.375
<b>what resides within that body</b>
<b>the personality, the soul.</b>

116
00:06:59.375 --> 00:07:03.083
<b>The same happens after death.</b>

117
00:07:03.083 --> 00:07:08.083
<b>No one can love a dead body for long,</b>

118
00:07:08.083 --> 00:07:11.666
<b>not even family members.</b>

119
00:07:11.666 --> 00:07:13.875
<b>All of this is</b>

120
00:07:13.875 --> 00:07:14.708
<b>because</b>

121
00:07:14.708 --> 00:07:19.500
<b>our true existence is not the body at all.</b>

122
00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:23.666
<b>Fundamentally, it is the soul that dwells within,</b>

123
00:07:23.666 --> 00:07:26.000
<b>and it is the soul that we love.</b>

124
00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.000
<b>And that</b>

125
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.708
<b>is our true existence.</b>

126
00:07:31.333 --> 00:07:35.583


127
00:07:35.583 --> 00:07:41.708
<b>We all know that our body</b>
<b>is constantly changing.</b>

128
00:07:41.708 --> 00:07:43.791
<b>A time will come</b>

129
00:07:43.791 --> 00:07:48.458
<b>when it will become weak and die.</b>

130
00:07:48.458 --> 00:07:50.583
<b>We know this,</b>

131
00:07:50.583 --> 00:07:51.750
<b>but</b>

132
00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:58.458
<b>the dilemma arises when</b>
<b>we refuse to accept this truth.</b>

133
00:07:58.458 --> 00:08:05.333
<b>We should not only know this truth</b>
<b>of change but also acknowledge it.</b>

134
00:08:05.333 --> 00:08:06.375
<b>Similarly,</b>

135
00:08:06.375 --> 00:08:08.083
<b>in professional life,</b>

136
00:08:08.083 --> 00:08:12.166
<b>change is a constant state.</b>

137
00:08:12.166 --> 00:08:14.541
<b>Just as we came forward, </b>

138
00:08:14.541 --> 00:08:16.416
<b>someone else will come too.</b>

139
00:08:16.416 --> 00:08:20.666
<b>Just as we took someone's vacant position,</b>

140
00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:25.083
<b>someone else will come and</b>
<b>sit in our vacant place.</b>

141
00:08:25.083 --> 00:08:32.000
<b>Our departure will not cause any</b>
<b>enterprise or organization to perish.</b>

142
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:36.541
<b>If we not only know this truth but also accept it,</b>

143
00:08:36.541 --> 00:08:40.250
<b>we can rise above unnecessary anxiety.</b>

144
00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:44.416
<b>At the same time, we can also</b>
<b>adopt the right perspective.</b>

145
00:08:44.416 --> 00:08:46.916
<b>By removing our ego from our position,</b>

146
00:08:46.916 --> 00:08:51.833
<b>we can build sweet</b>
<b>relationships with our colleagues.</b>

147
00:08:51.833 --> 00:08:54.166
<b>Such a spiritual perspective</b>

148
00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.875
<b> and such values will act as an anchor</b>

149
00:08:55.875 --> 00:09:04.791
<b>that keeps us steady in this</b>
<b>constantly turbulent ocean of professional life.</b>

